From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thehobbit85 <thehobbit85@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:09:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the selected Python when generating the Mac host

The NSP pipeline can run under the launcher's bundled Python while the
host Makefile finds an older python3 on PATH. Pass the pipeline's exact
interpreter to both Make invocations and quote it for the host shader
and profile generators. Direct Make builds keep python3 as their default.

Cover the actual host shader-header target with an unusable PATH Python
and a versioned interpreter in a directory with spaces. Verify both the
generation command and its dry run carry the exact interpreter.

Front-ends: No launcher change is required. The NSP pipeline keeps its
selected Python for host generation. Direct Make callers may set PYTHON.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: The Mac host Makefile can start an older PATH Python despite the launcher selecting a supported interpreter
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#711
